{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md | sed -n '390,560p'\"","aggregated_output":"   390\t  sourceAttachmentId: string | null;\n   391\t  relationshipKind: SourceProvenanceRelationship;\n   392\t  repositoryFullName: string;\n   393\t  repositoryUrl: string;\n   394\t  targetRef: string | null;\n   395\t  currentAttachmentDisplayName: string | null;\n   396\t  currentAttachmentScope: 'project' | 'process' | null;\n   397\t  currentAttachmentAccessMode: SourceAccessMode | null;\n   398\t  currentAttachmentHydrationState: HydrationState | null;\n   399\t  currentAttachmentVisibility: 'available' | 'detached' | 'unavailable' | 'redacted';\n   400\t  entryStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n   401\t  degradationReason: string | null;\n   402\t  recordedAt: string;\n   403\t}\n   404\t```\n   405\t\n   406\t### Routes\n   407\t\n   408\t| Operation | Method | Path | Service Method |\n   409\t|-----------|--------|------|----------------|\n   410\t| Attach project source | POST | `/api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments` | `attachProjectSource` |\n   411\t| Attach process source | POST | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/source-attachments` | `attachProcessSource` |\n   412\t| Update source | PATCH | `/api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments/:sourceAttachmentId` | `updateSource` |\n   413\t| Refresh source | POST | `/api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments/:sourceAttachmentId/refresh` | `refreshSource` |\n   414\t| Detach source | DELETE | `/api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments/:sourceAttachmentId` | `detachSource` |\n   415\t| Get process source provenance | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/source-provenance` | `listProcessSourceProvenance` |\n   416\t\n   417\tAll routes require authenticated access. Project-scoped routes call the existing\n   418\t`app.projectAccessService`; process-scoped attach/provenance reads also call\n   419\t`app.processAccessService`.\n   420\t\n   421\t### Error Codes\n   422\t\n   423\t| Status | Code | Meaning |\n   424\t|--------|------|---------|\n   425\t| 401 | `UNAUTHENTICATED` | Actor is missing |\n   426\t| 403 | `PROJECT_FORBIDDEN` | Actor lacks project access |\n   427\t| 403 | `PROCESS_FORBIDDEN` | Actor lacks process access |\n   428\t| 404 | `PROJECT_NOT_FOUND` | Project does not exist |\n   429\t| 404 | `PROCESS_NOT_FOUND` | Process does not exist in project |\n   430\t| 404 | `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_NOT_FOUND` | Source attachment does not exist in project |\n   431\t| 409 | `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_CONFLICT` | Active row already exists for same identity, scope, and target ref, or the update would violate writable-ref policy |\n   432\t| 409 | `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE` | Refresh cannot be accepted for this attachment state |\n   433\t| 422 | `INVALID_SOURCE_ATTACHMENT` | Request body, repository identity, or target-ref policy is invalid |\n   434\t| 503 | `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_UNAVAILABLE` | GitHub repository/ref cannot be accessed right now |\n   435\t\n   436\t## Service Interfaces\n   437\t\n   438\t```typescript\n   439\texport interface GitHubRepositoryResolver {\n   440\t  resolveRepository(args: {\n   441\t    repositoryUrl: string;\n   442\t    repositoryFullName?: string;\n   443\t    targetRef: string | null;\n   444\t  }): Promise<\n   445\t    | {\n   446\t        kind: 'resolved';\n   447\t        repositoryUrl: string;\n   448\t        repositoryFullName: string;\n   449\t        targetRef: string | null;\n   450\t      }\n   451\t    | { kind: 'invalid'; message: string }\n   452\t    | { kind: 'inaccessible'; message: string }\n   453\t  >;\n   454\t}\n   455\t\n   456\texport interface SourceManagementService {\n   457\t  attachProjectSource(args: {\n   458\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n   459\t    projectId: string;\n   460\t    input: CreateSourceAttachmentRequest;\n   461\t  }): Promise<SourceAttachmentSummary>;\n   462\t\n   463\t  attachProcessSource(args: {\n   464\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n   465\t    projectId: string;\n   466\t    processId: string;\n   467\t    input: CreateSourceAttachmentRequest;\n   468\t  }): Promise<SourceAttachmentSummary>;\n   469\t\n   470\t  updateSource(args: {\n   471\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n   472\t    projectId: string;\n   473\t    sourceAttachmentId: string;\n   474\t    input: UpdateSourceAttachmentRequest;\n   475\t  }): Promise<SourceAttachmentSummary>;\n   476\t\n   477\t  detachSource(args: {\n   478\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n   479\t    projectId: string;\n   480\t    sourceAttachmentId: string;\n   481\t  }): Promise<{ detached: true; sourceAttachmentId: string; detachedAt: string }>;\n   482\t}\n   483\t\n   484\texport interface SourceRefreshService {\n   485\t  refreshSource(args: {\n   486\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n   487\t    projectId: string;\n   488\t    sourceAttachmentId: string;\n   489\t  }): Promise<RefreshSourceAttachmentResponse>;\n   490\t}\n   491\t\n   492\texport interface SourceProvenanceService {\n   493\t  recordSourceProvenance(args: {\n   494\t    projectId: string;\n   495\t    processId: string;\n   496\t    sourceAttachmentId: string | null;\n   497\t    relationshipKind: SourceProvenanceRelationship;\n   498\t    repositoryFullName: string;\n   499\t    repositoryUrl: string;\n   500\t    targetRef: string | null;\n   501\t    eventId?: string | null;\n   502\t  }): Promise<SourceProvenanceEntry>;\n   503\t\n   504\t  listProcessSourceProvenance(args: {\n   505\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n   506\t    projectId: string;\n   507\t    processId: string;\n   508\t  }): Promise<{ entries: SourceProvenanceEntry[] }>;\n   509\t}\n   510\t```\n   511\t\n   512\t## Flow-by-Flow Design\n   513\t\n   514\t### Flow 1: Attach Repositories\n   515\t\n   516\tThis flow covers AC-1.1 through AC-1.4. The user attaches a GitHub repository\n   517\tfrom either the project shell or a process work surface. Fastify validates scope\n   518\tand repository identity before Convex persists the row.\n   519\t\n   520\t```mermaid\n   521\tsequenceDiagram\n   522\t    participant U as User\n   523\t    participant C as Client Source UI\n   524\t    participant R as Fastify Source Route\n   525\t    participant S as SourceManagementService\n   526\t    participant G as GitHubRepositoryResolver\n   527\t    participant P as PlatformStore\n   528\t    participant X as Convex\n   529\t\n   530\t    U->>C: Submit repository URL and metadata\n   531\t    C->>R: POST source-attachments\n   532\t    Note over R,S: AC-1.1: project or process scoped attach\n   533\t    R->>S: attachProjectSource or attachProcessSource\n   534\t    S->>G: resolveRepository(url, fullName?, targetRef)\n   535\t    Note over S,G: AC-1.4: reject invalid/inaccessible repos\n   536\t    G-->>S: canonical repositoryFullName\n   537\t    S->>P: createSourceAttachment\n   538\t    P->>X: sourceAttachments:createSourceAttachment\n   539\t    Note over P,X: AC-1.3: duplicate active row rejected\n   540\t    alt Process-scoped attach\n   541\t        S->>P: add sourceAttachmentId to current process source refs\n   542\t    end\n   543\t    X-->>P: persisted row\n   544\t    P-->>S: SourceAttachmentSummary\n   545\t    S-->>R: summary\n   546\t    R-->>C: 201 summary\n   547\t```\n   548\t\n   549\tFor process-scoped attach, `SourceManagementService` must update the process's\n   550\tcurrent source refs so the new source appears immediately in\n   551\t`materials.currentSources`. Project-scoped attach creates a durable shared\n   552\tsource row but does not automatically make that source current for every\n   553\tprocess.\n   554\t\n   555\t### Flow 2: Manage Purpose, Access Mode, and Target Ref\n   556\t\n   557\tThis flow covers AC-2.1 through AC-2.4. Purpose and access mode are durable\n   558\tmetadata. Target ref is part of the source definition; changing it marks a\n   559\tpreviously hydrated attachment stale until refresh/rehydration catches up.\n   560\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
